<title>CHILE: Drug-maker LabChile restructures debt.</title>
<headline>Drug-maker LabChile restructures debt.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical company Laboratorio Chile said Friday it had received a $60 million long-term loan to repay its short-term debts.</p>
<p>The loan was made by a group of banks including Rabobank, ING Barings, American Express Bank and Dresdner Bank, it said the statement.</p>
<p>LabChile is Chile's largest pharmaceutical manufacturer.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago Newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212))</p>
</text>
